# Player, Camera, and Input

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M1 Technical proofs
Dependencies: `01_PROJECT_FOUNDATION.todo`

## Purpose

Prove responsive third-person movement and visually honest aiming before territory complexity is added.

## Tasks

- [ ] Implement camera-relative movement.
- [ ] Implement acceleration, deceleration, gravity, and grounded state.
- [ ] Implement independent camera look and aim.
- [ ] Implement over-the-shoulder camera collision.
- [ ] Implement keyboard/mouse actions.
- [ ] Implement gamepad actions.
- [ ] Implement sensitivity and inversion settings.
- [ ] Implement world-space aim solution.
- [ ] Implement debug ray/contact visualization.
- [ ] Define external impulse and status-modifier hooks.
- [ ] Add movement and camera PlayMode tests.
- [ ] Profile allocations and frame cost.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Controller feels responsive in the sandbox at 60 FPS.
- [ ] Reticle, physics contact, and spray target derive from the same aim solution.
- [ ] Camera does not remain inside arena geometry.
- [ ] Keyboard/mouse and gamepad are both usable.
- [ ] No recurring managed allocation after warm-up.
- [ ] Settings persist locally.

